wifi: brcmfmac: Add DMI nvram filename quirk for Chuwi Vi8 Plus with unfilled DMI

Some Chuwi Vi8 Plus (CWI519) units report "To be filled by O.E.M." for both
sys_vendor and product_name, so the fallback board_type built from those two
fields becomes a name no nvram file will ever have, and the radio never
initialises.

The nvram which linux-firmware carries for this tablet,
brcmfmac43430-sdio.Hampoo-D2D3_Vi8A1.txt, only exists under the revision-less
name and so is unreachable on a chip-revision 0 (a0) unit, which looks for
brcmfmac43430a0-sdio.*. Both revisions shipped in this model. Point the quirk
at ilife-S806 instead, which is present as an a0 build and is the same AP6212
module; the chiprev check keeps a1 units on their existing path.

Tested on an a0 unit, where the Vi8 Plus nvram data is confirmed to work.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
---
 Generated against linux master 3eb40771c00a (2026-08-15).
 Apply with: git am, or patch -p1 < this file
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/dmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/dmi.c
@@ -34,6 +34,16 @@
 	BRCM_CC_43430_CHIP_ID, 0, "ilife-S806"
 };
 
+/* The Chuwi Vi8 Plus uses the same Ampak AP6212 module as the Chuwi Hi8 Pro.
+ * Units with a chip-revision 0 (a0) radio cannot use the nvram which is in
+ * linux-firmware under the Vi8 Plus' own name, because that is only present
+ * under the revision-less name; the ilife-S806 file is the a0 build of the
+ * same data.
+ */
+static const struct brcmf_dmi_data chuwi_vi8_plus_data = {
+	BRCM_CC_43430_CHIP_ID, 0, "ilife-S806"
+};
+
 static const struct brcmf_dmi_data gpd_win_pocket_data = {
 	BRCM_CC_4356_CHIP_ID, 2, "gpd-win-pocket"
 };
@@ -116,6 +126,16 @@
 		.driver_data = (void *)&chuwi_hi8_pro_data,
 	},
 	{
+		/* Chuwi Vi8 Plus (CWI519) with unfilled system DMI */
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "Hampoo"),
+			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "Cherry Trail CR"),
+			/* Above strings are too generic, also match on BIOS date */
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BIOS_DATE, "12/11/2015"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = (void *)&chuwi_vi8_plus_data,
+	},
+	{
 		/* Cyberbook T116 rugged tablet */
 		.matches = {
 			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "Default string"),
